From 1957a0a709be477a2914d8535ac963cb462d1a9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bert Outtier <bert.outtier@spectricity.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:59:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(network_adapter): authorize the station port if auth done
 fails

With WPA2, the host driver asks for a control port and sends
CMD_STA_SET_AUTHORIZED after the 4-way handshake. On ESP32-C3 with
ESP-IDF v6.1, esp_wifi_auth_done_internal() fails at that point, so the
command fails, station_authorized stays 0 and all data except EAPOL is
dropped: the station is associated but gets no IP address.

This started with the move to ESP-IDF v6.1 (merge 4ddec53): it works with
ffe2af4, built with ESP-IDF v5.5.1, while the firmware code for this
command did not change.

Log a warning and authorize the port anyway, the keys are installed.
---
 esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/cmd.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/cmd.c b/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/cmd.c
index c4ffeef..f49450f 100644
--- a/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/cmd.c
+++ b/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/cmd.c
@@ -2736,10 +2736,16 @@ int process_sta_set_authorized(uint8_t if_type, uint8_t *payload,
         ESP_LOGD(TAG, "STA_PORT_AUTH_DONE seq=%u ipc_failed=%u",
                  active_cmd_seq, auth_done_failed);
         if (auth_done_failed) {
-            cmd_status = CMD_RESPONSE_FAIL;
-        } else {
-            station_authorized = 1;
+            /*
+             * With the Wi-Fi libraries of ESP-IDF v6.1 this fails although
+             * the host completed the 4-way handshake and installed the keys,
+             * which left the data path closed for good. Open the port
+             * anyway: the keys are in place, so data can flow.
+             */
+            ESP_LOGW(TAG, "STA_PORT_AUTH seq=%u auth done failed, authorizing anyway",
+                     active_cmd_seq);
         }
+        station_authorized = 1;
     } else {
         /* Deauthorization changes port authorization status without tearing
          * down the 802.11 association. Do not disconnect the peer. */
-- 
2.53.0

